{"availability":"available","full":"CogniBlock/CogniBlock","name":"CogniBlock","description":"Visual image-pipeline playground: drag blocks, wire them up and watch every step run live in your browser. Open engine package, share links and a Solana community token.","category":"Other","language":"HTML","stars":10,"forks":1,"created":"2026-10-03T15:33:43Z","updated":"2026-10-03T18:37:47Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://cogniblock.net/","topics":["agi","ai","pipeline"],"demo":"https://cogniblock.netlify.app/pipelines.html","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:23.554Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:23.554Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:23.554Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:16:23.554Z","stars":10,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["CogniBlock makes a pipeline something you can see. Instead of reading code to understand what happens to an image, you build it from blocks: each block does one job, you wire them together, and every block shows a live preview of its own result.","Pick a picture, add Canny Edge to trace its outlines, Blur to soften them, Blend to glow them back over the original, and watch the picture change as you move a slider. Then download the result or send a link to anyone.","Everything runs in the browser. No server crunches your images, no account is needed, and nothing you load ever leaves your device."],"features":["Why it is worth a look","How a pipeline works","Use the engine as a package","Security and privacy","What we are exploring next"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/CogniBlock/CogniBlock/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"44be29a66a448be1e09c78ee41b6484d4de508e4965e4562107476b8fb034841","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T06:12:38.605Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:12:38.605Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"CogniBlock makes a pipeline something you can see. Instead of reading code to understand what happens to an image, you b